  "chapter": {
    "number": 109,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(110) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord said to my Lord, Sit you on my right hand, until I make your enemies your footstool.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord shall send out a rod of power for you out of Sion: rule you in the midst of your enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "With you is dominion in the day of your power, in the splendors of",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 208
          },
          {
            "text": "your saints: I have begotten you from the womb before the morning.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord swore, and will not repent, You are a priest for ever, after the order of Melchisedec.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord at your right hand has dashed in pieces kings in the day of his wrath.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He shall judge among the nations, he shall fill up the number of corpses, he shall crush the heads of many on the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He shall drink of the brook in the way; therefore shall he lift up the head.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 208,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, holiness, i.e. holy things.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 109,
          "verse": 3
        }
      }
    ]
  },
